      "message": "In this CL, speed feature ‘adaptive_luma_loop_filter_skip’ is tuned to improve the visual quality for lc-dec mode. As the blocking artifacts were seen primarily in higher pyramid-level frames (levels 5 and 6), we tuned the loop-filter disabling logic by lowering the ‘filter_threshold’ (below which the filter level is set to 0) from 32 to 16 for these pyramid levels. With this change, we observed no visual artifacts.\nThe tests are performed on commit 2a70ad7b (dated 26 Sept). We validated that the patch does not conflict with the latest version.\nThe performance results of vertical 608p/720p clips with low complexity decode mode enabled are given below:\n```\n                        Instruction Count                                                                 \n                           Reduction(%)                        BD-Rate Loss(%)                  Time Reduction(%)\ncpu-used  Resolution    Encoder   Decoder    avg.psnr   ovr.psnr    ssim      vmaf    vmaf_neg    dav1d Decoder   \n   1         608p        0.069    -1.298     -0.0494   -0.0480    -0.0716    0.0429    0.0096       -1.111\n   2         608p       -0.012    -1.244     -0.0585   -0.0628    -0.0688    0.0113    0.0227       -1.074\n   3         608p       -0.007    -1.244     -0.0423   -0.0522    -0.0580   -0.0438   -0.0179       -1.700\n   1         720p       -0.121    -1.561     -0.0602   -0.0571    -0.0711    0.0296    0.0087       -1.280\n   2         720p       -0.055    -1.534     -0.0559   -0.0497    -0.0660    0.0081    0.0066       -1.343\n   3         720p       -0.009    -1.478     -0.0479   -0.0527    -0.0631    0.0041   -0.0067       -1.279\n```\nThe performance results of vertical 608p/720p clips with low complexity decode mode enabled w.r.t lc-dec\u003d0 are given below:\n```\n                        Instruction Count                                                                 \n                           Reduction(%)                        BD-Rate Loss(%) 